1.Explain hidden state in RNN. Describe how hidden state stores previous information.

The hidden state ℎ𝑡 is the internal memory of an RNN that captures information from previous timesteps
It stores context by combining the current input 𝑥𝑡 and the previous hidden state ℎ𝑡−1
Each new hidden state depends on both the current input and the past hidden state,enabling the network to 'remember'
prior information across time.

