2.Explain how an RNN reads the sentence word by word using time steps.
Example:  
food was not good

RNN process sequences one word at a time using timesteps
For the sentence "food was not good"

At 𝑡1:input ="food", output =ℎ1
At 𝑡2:input ="was", output =ℎ2(depends on ℎ1)
At 𝑡3:input ="not", output =ℎ3(depends on ℎ2)
At 𝑡4:input ="good", output =ℎ4(depends on ℎ3)

This sequential dependency allows the model to understand context and word order.

