4.Explain the role of input vector, previous hidden state, weights, and bias in RNN.

Input vector xt - Represent current data point(eg.word embedding)
Previous Hidden State ℎ𝑡−1 - Carries memory from earlier steps
Weights W - Learn how input and past states interact
Bias b - Shift activation to improve learning flexibility

